# Local fast-feedback gate — the same guard rails CI enforces as `lint-and-typecheck`,
# run before code leaves this machine. Convenience, not enforcement: skippable with
# `git push --no-verify` or by a clone that never ran `npm install`. The non-bypassable
# gate is the required status check on `main` (docs/FRAMEWORK.md ➜ "Guard rails").

echo ""
echo "──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"
echo " pre-push: checking framework guard rails (npm run check)"
echo "   • NO raw Playwright locators or 'new *Page()' in tests/**/*.spec.ts"
echo "       — selectors live on Page Objects, reached through the fixture"
echo "   • NO expect(...) inside src/pages/**  — assertions live in specs"
echo "   • tsc --noEmit must pass"
echo "──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"
echo ""

if npm run --silent check; then
  echo ""
  echo " ✔ guard rails passed — pushing."
  echo ""
  exit 0
fi

cat >&2 <<'EOF'

 ✖ PUSH BLOCKED — a framework guard rail failed (see the errors above).

   This is the same check CI runs as 'lint-and-typecheck', so pushing would
   only fail there too. How to fix the common ones:

   • "Raw locator .locator(...) / .getByRole(...) is not allowed in a test"
       → add the selector as an arrow-function property on a Page Object in
         src/pages/**, and call it via the injected fixture, e.g.
         homePage.findTrainsForm.fromStationInput()

   • "Assertions belong in tests, not Page Objects"
       → return a Locator or a plain value from the Page Object and put the
         expect(...) in the spec

   • Type errors → run 'npm run typecheck' for the full list

   Re-check locally:            npm run check
   Emergency override (never on a shared branch):   git push --no-verify

EOF
exit 1
